  </script-output|<image|<tuple|<#>|ps>||||>>>|<label|fig:iteration>The
  iteration<nbsp><eqref|eq:iteration>, schematically, with only two external
  legs drawn per vertex. Each step inserts the previous correction into the
  trace and gains one loop and one factor <math|g<rsub|q>>, as
  in<nbsp><eqref|eq:increments>. After two steps the defect is the trace
  difference of order <math|g<rsub|q><rsup|3>>, which
  gives<nbsp><eqref|eq:defect-bound> and makes the source integrable in the
  backward equation.>

  <paragraph|The quadratic part> The low jets are not iterated: they are
  handled exactly by the path <math|M>. The quadratic part of the flow at
  <math|y=0> is, by evenness, <math|<frac|1|2>*D<rsup|2><math-up|Tr>H<around|(|0|)>=-<frac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|R<rsub|0><rsup|2>>D<rsup|4>*\<Gamma\><rsup|<math-up|o>><around|(|0|)>>,
  where <math|R<rsub|0,q>=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsub|q>|)><rsup|-1>> and
  <math|<math-up|Ctr><rsub|R>T> contracts two slots of <math|T> with the
  kernel <math|R>. Requiring that <math|M> solves this part of the flow
  exactly gives the <em|mass equation>

  <\equation>
    <label|eq:mass>\<partial\><rsub|q>*M<rsub|q>=B<rsub|q><around|[|M|]>\<assign\>-\<gamma\><math-up|Tr><around*|(|R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2>|)>*I-<tfrac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2>>D<rsup|4>*h<rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q><around|(|0|)>,
  </equation>

  (the source <math|B<rsub|q><around|[|M|]>> is not the sampling Brownian
  motion <math|B>), with the <em|mixed boundary conditions>

  <\equation*>
    \<mu\><rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>=b,<space|2em>\<Theta\><rsub|q>\<to\>0*<text|as
    >q\<to\>\<infty\>
  </equation*>

  (the latter in first spatial moment). The running mass is pinned at the
  auxiliary scale <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>, at a value <math|b> with
  <math|\|b\|\<leqslant\> B\<gamma\> q<rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|1/2>>, while the
  nonlocal kernel is pinned at infinity. The bare mass is then

  <\equation>
    <label|eq:bare-mass>\<mu\><rsub|N>=lim<rsub|q\<to\>\<infty\>>
    \<mu\><rsub|q>=b+<big|int><rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>><rsup|\<infty\>>\<beta\><rsub|q><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>q,<space|2em>B<rsub|q>*<with|math-font|Bbb|1>=\<beta\><rsub|q>*<with|math-font|Bbb|1>,
  </equation>

  and it is this number that enters the Gibbs measure<nbsp><eqref|eq:nuN>.
  Note the order: the counterterm is an output of the deterministic flow, not
  an input.

  <\proposition>
    <dueto|The coefficient construction<nbsp><cite|FBSDE26>><label|prop:coeff>
    For <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>> large enough (depending on <math|\<gamma\>>,
    not on <math|N>), the system<nbsp><eqref|eq:iteration>\U<eqref|eq:mass>
    has a unique solution in a ball, with

    <\equation>
      <label|eq:coeff><around|\||\<mu\><rsub|q>|\|>\<leqslant\>C*\<gamma\>*<sqrt|q>,<space|2em>v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\><rsub|q>|)>\<leqslant\>C*\<gamma\><rsup|2>*q<rsup|-1/2>,<space|2em><around|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|q>*M<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>\<leqslant\>C*g<rsub|q>,
    </equation>

    where <math|v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\>|)>=<big|int>d<around|(|0,z|)>*<around|\||\<Theta\>*<around|(|0,z|)>|\|>\<mathd\>z>.
    The seed obeys <math|\<cal-N\><rsub|k,q><around|(|\<cal-L\>|)>\<leqslant\>C<rsub|k>*g<rsub|q>*q*r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>>,
    <math|4\<leqslant\>k\<leqslant\>10>, and the corrections obey

    <\equation>
      <label|eq:increments>\<cal-N\><rsub|k,q>*<around*|(|h<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>-h<rsup|<around|[|j-1|]>>|)>\<leqslant\>C<rsub|k>*<space|0.17em>g<rsub|q><rsup|j+1>*<space|0.17em>q*<space|0.17em>r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>,<space|2em>4\<leqslant\>k\<leqslant\>10-2*j,<space|1em>j=1,2,
    </equation>

    where <math|\<cal-N\><rsub|k,q><around|(|f|)>=<math-ss|S><rsub|k><around|(|f|)>+<sqrt|q>*<space|0.17em>v<rsub|1>*<around|(|D<rsup|k>*f<around|(|0|)>|)>>,
    and for a <math|k>-tensor

    <\equation*>
      v<rsub|1><around|(|T|)>=max<rsub|i,a\<less\>b> sup<rsub|x<rsub|i>>
      <big|int>d<around|(|x<rsub|a>,x<rsub|b>|)><around|\||T|\|>*<big|prod><rsub|j\<ne\>i>\<mathd\>x<rsub|j>.
    </equation*>

    The complete defect of <math|\<Gamma\><rsup|<math-up|o>>> on the ball is
    <math|e<rsup|<math-up|o>><rsub|q>=\<Pi\>*<around|(|\<cal-T\><rsub|q>*<around|[|M,h<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|]>-\<cal-T\><rsub|q>*<around|[|M,h<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|]>|)>>,
    and

    <\equation>
      <label|eq:defect-bound><math-ss|S><rsub|4><around*|(|e<rsup|<math-up|o>><rsub|q>|)>\<leqslant\>C*\<gamma\><rsup|5>*q<rsup|-3>.
    </equation>

    At fixed <math|N> the bare mass exists,
    <math|\|\<mu\><rsub|N>-b\|\<lesssim\>\<gamma\><math-up|Tr>C<rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>\<lesssim\>\<gamma\>N>,
    and <math|<around|\||\<mu\><rsub|N>-\<mu\><rsub|q>|\|>\<leqslant\>C*\<gamma\>*N<rsup|3>/q>,
    <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<Theta\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>\<leqslant\>C*N*\<gamma\><rsup|2>*q<rsup|-1/2>\<to\>0>
    as <math|q\<to\>\<infty\>>.
  </proposition>

  <\render-proof|Idea of the proof>
    (a) <em|Trace Lipschitz estimate.> If two corrections <math|h,<wide|h|^>>
    obey the individual bounds<nbsp><eqref|eq:power-counting> up to order
    <math|k+2> and their difference obeys them with <math|g<rsub|q>> replaced
    by <math|\<varepsilon\><rsub|q>>, then
    <math|\<cal-N\><rsub|k>*<around|(|\<cal-T\>*<around|[|M,h|]>-\<cal-T\>*<around|[|M,<wide|h|^>|]>|)>\<leqslant\>C*\<varepsilon\><rsub|q>*q<rsup|1/2>*r<rsub|q><rsup|-k>>.
    Expand <math|D<rsup|k>> of the trace into loops; in each, telescope the
    difference onto one marked vertex or propagator and
    apply<nbsp><eqref|eq:loop>. (b) <em|Integration.> Each step gains one
    <math|g>; the integrand of<nbsp><eqref|eq:iteration> is
    <math|O<around|(|\<gamma\><rsup|1+k/2>*s<rsup|-k/2>|)>> in the <math|k>th
    derivative, and that of the increment
    <math|h<rsup|<around|[|j+1|]>>-h<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>> is
    <math|O<around|(|\<gamma\><rsup|1+k/2>*s<rsup|-k/2>*g<rsub|s><rsup|j>|)>>,
    integrable at <math|s=\<infty\>> for <math|k\<geqslant\>4>. The low jets
    have been removed, so the lower derivatives are controlled by Taylor's
    formula from the fourth. (c) <em|Mass path.> Given <math|M> in the ball,
    the right side of<nbsp><eqref|eq:mass> is computed from the corrections,
    and the map <math|M\<mapsto\><around|(|\<mu\>,\<Theta\>|)>> is a
    contraction for large <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>: differences gain a factor
    <math|g<rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>> (for <math|\<mu\>> after integrating from
    <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>, using <math|sup<rsub|x> log
    x/<sqrt|x>\<less\>\<infty\>>). (d) <em|Defect.> The mass equation
    supplies exactly the quadratic jet of the flow, and
    <math|\<partial\><rsub|q>*h<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>=\<Pi\>*\<cal-T\>*<around|[|M,h<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|]>>,
    so the defect is the trace difference between the last two
    approximations, of order <math|g<rsup|3>>: by (a) with
    <math|\<varepsilon\><rsub|q>=g<rsub|q><rsup|3>>,
    <math|<math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|e<rsup|<math-up|o>>|)>\<leqslant\>C*g<rsub|q><rsup|3>*q<rsup|1/2>*r<rsub|q><rsup|-4>=C*\<gamma\><rsup|5>*q<rsup|-3>>.
  </render-proof>

  Two technical points are hidden in this sketch. First, the trace estimate
  (a) needs more derivatives than it controls: the <math|k>th derivative of
  the trace involves vertices of order <math|k+2>. Ten derivatives of the
  seed leave eight after one step and six after two; this is why the number
  of steps must be finite and fixed in advance (an infinite iteration loses
  all derivatives). Second, the quadratic kernel <math|\<Theta\><rsub|q>>
  must be measured in a first spatial moment <math|v<rsub|1>>, not in a
  second one: the estimate <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<delta\><rsub|z><rsup|2>*C<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>\<lesssim\>d<around|(|0,z|)><rsup|2>>,
  which a second moment would require, fails by a logarithm, and one uses
  <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<delta\><rsub|z><rsup|2>*C<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|-1/2>*d<around|(|0,z|)>>
  instead<nbsp><cite|FBSDE26>. This is also why <math|\<cal-N\><rsub|k>>
  contains a spatial moment at <math|y=0>.

  <subsection|Two mass renormalisations>

  The bare mass <math|\<mu\><rsub|N>> diverges as <math|N\<to\>\<infty\>>.
  Its two divergent parts are the two divergent self-energy diagrams of
  Appendix<nbsp><hlink|A.2|cqft_lecture4.tm#sec:pert> of Lecture<nbsp>4.

  <\itemize>
    <item><em|The tadpole.> The first term of<nbsp><eqref|eq:mass> integrates
    to <math|-\<gamma\>*<big|int><rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>><rsup|\<infty\>><math-up|Tr>R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>q\<approx\>-\<gamma\><math-up|Tr>C=-3*\<lambda\><math-up|Tr>C\<sim\>-N>
    (up to a term independent of <math|N>). This is Wick ordering:
    <math|<frac|\<lambda\>|4>*\<varphi\><rsup|4>-<frac|3|2>*\<lambda\>*c*\<varphi\><rsup|2>>
    agrees, up to a constant, with <math|<frac|\<lambda\>|4>*H<rsub|4>*<around|(|\<varphi\>;c|)>>,
    with <math|c=C*<around|(|x,x|)>> (<hlink|(A.5)|cqft_lecture4.tm#eq:first-order>
    of Lecture<nbsp>4).

    <item><em|The sunset.> The second term contracts the bubble contained in
    <math|D<rsup|4>*h<rsup|<around|[|2|]>><around|(|0|)>> (the quartic
    coefficient of the seed) with <math|R<rsub|0><rsup|2>>, and integrating
    in <math|q> produces the two-loop self-energy, which diverges like
    <math|\<lambda\><rsup|2>*<big|int><rsub|<around|\||z|\|>\<gtr\>1/N><around|\||z|\|><rsup|-3>\<mathd\>z\<sim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>*log
    N>. This is the sunset counterterm <math|\<gamma\><rsub|T>\<sim\>log T>
    of <hlink|(A.7)|cqft_lecture4.tm#eq:gammaT> of Lecture<nbsp>4: with
    <math|\<lambda\><rsub|<math-up|L3>>=\<lambda\>/4> and
    <math|\<gamma\><rsub|T>*<big|int>H<rsub|2>=\<gamma\><rsub|T>*<big|int>\<varphi\><rsup|2>+>const,
    the sunset part of <math|\<mu\><rsub|N>> is
    <math|2*\<gamma\><rsub|T>=6*\<lambda\><rsup|2>*<big|int>C<rsup|3>\<approx\><frac|3*\<lambda\><rsup|2>|8*\<pi\><rsup|2>>*log
    N>, positive. (The double-tadpole logarithms in the two terms
    of<nbsp><eqref|eq:mass>, the bubble with a tadpole insertion and the mass
    insertion in <math|<math-up|Tr>R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2>>, cancel each other.)
  </itemize>

  <big-figure|<with|par-mode|center|<\script-output|tikz|default>
    \\documentclass[tikz]{standalone}

    \\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}

    \\usepackage[sc]{mathpazo}

    \\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}

    \\usetikzlibrary{calc,decorations.markings}

    \\tikzset{

    \ blob/.style={circle,draw,thick,fill=#1,minimum size=7mm,inner sep=0pt},

    \ blob/.default={black!12},

    \ vtx/.style={circle,fill=black,inner sep=1.5pt},

    \ prop/.style={thick},

    \ full/.style={double,double distance=1.3pt,thick},

    \ ins/.style={circle,fill=black,inner sep=1.5pt},

