    <\associate|figure>
      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|10.1>||The structure of
      the construction. The two arrows between the forward and backward
      estimates form the closed loop of Lecture
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>>6:
      neither estimate closes on its own.>|<pageref|auto-10>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|11.1>||The seed
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:seed>)>
      as one-loop graphs: lines <with|mode|<quote|math>|C<rsub|q>>, and a
      vertex <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<gamma\> y<rsup|2>> with its two
      external fields at each corner. The <with|mode|<quote|math>|j>-th ring
      has <with|mode|<quote|math>|2j> legs and coefficient
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|(-1)<rsup|j+1>/(2j)>. The series sums to a
      logarithm and has radius of convergence
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|r<rsub|q>>. The quartic ring is the
      bubble.>|<pageref|auto-16>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|11.2>||The iteration
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:iteration>)>,
      schematically, with only two external legs drawn per vertex. Each step
      inserts the previous correction into the trace and gains one loop and
      one factor <with|mode|<quote|math>|g<rsub|q>>, as in
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:increments>)>.
      After two steps the defect is the trace difference of order
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|g<rsub|q><rsup|3>>, which gives
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:defect-bound>)>
      and makes the source integrable in the backward
      equation.>|<pageref|auto-18>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|11.3>||The mass
      equation <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:mass>)>
      and the two divergent parts of the bare mass. The cross is the
      insertion <with|mode|<quote|math>|R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2>>. Since
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|D<rsup|4>h<rsup|[2]>(0)> contains the bubble of
      Figure <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|fig:seed-rings>,
      its contraction contains the sunset. Integrating in
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|q> turns the crossed line into a line
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|C>: the tadpole is linear in
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|N> and the sunset
      logarithmic.>|<pageref|auto-21>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|12.1>||The force on one
      site, for <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<lambda\>=1>,
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|q=4>. Left: the frozen cube leaves the exact
      force at <with|mode|<quote|math>|x\<sim\>r<rsub|q>>, while the
      integrated cube follows it at all fields. Right: the remainder of the
      frozen cube grows like the cube itself, while the remainder of the
      integrated cube stays below the bound of Theorem
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|thm:pl-global>.>|<pageref|auto-37>>
    </associate>
